{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of the pataḥ of the bet in במקום.</b> The words of Moses [Maimonides], and the meaning is \"in the known place\" — that day, and so Hosea said, \"and there He will speak with us\" (Hosea 12:5), for he prophesied concerning Jeroboam son of Joash, and he was in Bethel, and he used plural language on his own behalf and on behalf of Amos, and in the book of Amos it is made clear. And according to the plain sense it is impossible for it to be ויפגע, like \"do not intercede on my behalf\" (Jeremiah 7:16), for we do not find in Scripture that HaShem is called \"Place,\" and do not set your mind on the derash of ממקום אחר (Esther 4:14), for it is not at all about the Name, and the word אחר is superfluous:" "<b>From the stones of the place.</b> Its meaning: one of the stones of the place." "<b>At his headrest.</b> Plural form, like \"at his feet\" (Ruth 3:4, 8), and the puzzle is from Rabbi Samuel, who mixed the dreams of human beings with the dream of prophecy:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Resolved 'דברי משה' as referring to Moses Maimonides (Guide of the Perplexed I.III.8), based on the well-known attribution of the 'Place' identification to Maimonides in medieval Hebrew commentary; the phrase 'והוא היה בבית אל' appears to refer to Hosea, not Jeroboam."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:11.905025335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}